2. Silicon Canvas
   Copyright (c) 2026 Jiale Wang
   https://github.com/du-du-wang/silicon-canvas, commit 7b590daf2217acc5a95d5c40d289d56d91a9fbfc
   MIT License: scripts/lib/engine/silicon/LICENSE

   scripts/lib/engine/silicon/*.js are a translation into JavaScript of 24 modules of
   src/silicon_canvas/ of that commit, made by a source-to-source translator
   (tools/port/transpile.py in the draw-diagram repository, not shipped with the skill)
   from that source with two modifications:
       publication_render.py  font() measures text with scripts/data/widths.json
                              (Helvetica metrics) instead of the bundled Noto font
       structure_scene.py     label placement measures text the same way and needs
                              no font file or image
   scripts/lib/engine/silicon/catalog.json and reference_images/*.json are copied from
   src/silicon_canvas/ without modification.
   The repository keeps the Python source, the diff of the two modifications and the
   upstream record under tools/port/silicon/.

   Written for this skill to run the translation: scripts/lib/engine/py/ (Python
   semantics for JavaScript), scripts/lib/engine/fast/ (a faster equivalent of one
   function) and scripts/lib/engine/js.js; they are not part of Silicon Canvas.


